  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1809.02 Specific Requirements for Enclosure of RACM",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1809.02 Specific Requirements for Enclosure of RACM. When an owner or operator chooses to abate RACM via enclosure, the owner or operator shall comply with the requirements of Env-A 1808 and the following:\n\n(a) Ensure that enclosures are airtight and of permanent construction, such that the area being enclosed is inaccessible;\n\n(b) Prior to commencing work, wet all RACM that has the potential to be disturbed during the installation of hangers, brackets, or other portions of the enclosure; and\n\n(c) Designate enclosures for RACM by posting permanent signs, labels, color coding, or some other readily visible mechanism on the enclosure to warn individuals who may be required to disturb the enclosure.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, Revision Note #2, and Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-A 1800) #14104, eff 11-1-24, EXPIRES: 11-1-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a1800.html"
